Architecture Diagram
Description: Design a diagram showing how the Bus Tracker hardware and software communicate.
Tasks:
- Include IR sensors, Raspberry Pi, MQTT, backend API, database, and front-end app.
- Show how passenger data moves through the system.
- Include capacity checking and the overcrowding alarm.
Acceptance criteria:
- All main components are included.
- Data flow is clearly shown.
- Driver and passenger interfaces are connected to the system.
2. Database Design
Description: Design a database to store bus details and passenger entry/exit events.
Tasks:
- Create the Bus and Event table designs.
- Define primary keys and foreign keys.
- Plan how to calculate passenger occupancy.
Acceptance criteria:
- Tables and relationships are documented.
- Entry/exit events include timestamps and bus IDs.
- The database supports current occupancy and recent activity queries.
